 {
  "id": "G114",
  "article_id": "gnews:bdcb0ed0921c2e9ae241083c",
  "title": "Palantir’s NVIDIA AI Collab Could Be a Game-Changer That Marks a Turn in the Stock",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-03",
  "article_opening": "Palantir shares surged 18% in a week as investors rotate from semis into AI software.\nA new deal using Nvidia's Nemotron to build government AI models squeezes short sellers and may justify Palantir's 145x trailing P/E multiple.\nDespite Palantir's 85% revenue growth quarter, Nvidia may offer better value.\nShares of Palantir ( NASDAQ:PLTR ) have been bouncing back, now up close to 18% in a week, and it might be a good idea to step out of the way if you're short or are hanging onto bearish put opt",
  "passage": "Palantir shares surged 18% in a week as investors rotate from semis into AI software.\nA new deal using Nvidia's Nemotron to build government AI models squeezes short sellers and may justify Palantir's 145x trailing P/E multiple.\nDespite Palantir's 85% revenue growth quarter, Nvidia may offer better value.\nShares of Palantir ( NASDAQ:PLTR ) have been bouncing back, now up close to 18% in a week, and it might be a good idea to step out of the way if you're short or are hanging onto bearish put options. Dr. Michael Burry recently announced that he'd covered half of his short position around a week ago, a move that's proved incredibly well-timed. As investors pile back into the AI software plays and away from the semiconductors, I do think that Palantir stands out as a name that might not take all too long before it's at fresh highs again.\nWhile Palantir's stock is still wildly expensive, one has to think that CEO Ale…",
